# Yumii — Configuration

## ⚠️  Do NOT create a .env file to configure Yumii.

Yumii stores API keys in **~/.yumii/auth.json** (an owner-only local file,
the same model Claude Code and opencode use) and preferences in
~/.yumii/config.json. A .env file has **no effect** — the app never reads it.

## How to configure Yumii

- **Installing:** the installer (`iex (irm https://yumii.me/install.ps1)`)
  asks you to pick her mind, ears and voice and to paste one API key — by
  default a Nebius Token Factory key for NVIDIA Nemotron
  (https://tokenfactory.nebius.com/project/api-keys).
- **From source:** run the desktop app (`cd desktop && npx @tauri-apps/cli dev`);
  the first-run card asks for the key.
- **Any time after:** the dashboard (tray icon → Dashboard → Settings) changes
  providers, personality, voice and keys — including an optional
  TAVILY_API_KEY for Tavily-powered web search.

All API keys are stored in ~/.yumii/auth.json with owner-only permissions.
